{"runId":"2026-10-31T11-31-02-552Z","seq":23,"at":"2026-10-31T11:32:08.040Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"constraint_contradicted","severity":"blocking","claim":"Require attack-free training/calibration, authorised access, Yocto on-device execution within agreed budgets, and no measurable forwarding-latency increase under agreed representative loads.","sources":[{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"A few of them have been running their networks for twenty years with no security monitoring at all, so if they were compromised they would not know.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"},{"recordId":"C001-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"We have plenty of normal traffic — we have collected several terabytes of captures from consenting clients over the past three years — but we have nothing labelled as malicious.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"Requiring attack-free training and calibration makes the pilot depend on a cleanliness guarantee the company cannot provide, contradicting the proposal's own treatment of the archives as unlabelled. Require no attack-labelled training or calibration instead, and explicitly assess sensitivity to possible contamination.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
